  "services": {
    "perplexity": {
      "description": "The Harder They Come (Original Soundtrack Recording), released in 1972 on Island Records, is a landmark album that introduced reggae music to a global audience. Centered around the film of the same name, the album features performances by the film’s star, Jimmy Cliff, alongside seminal reggae artists such as Desmond Dekker, Toots and the Maytals, The Melodians, and The Slickers. The musical style is rooted in classic reggae and rocksteady, with tracks showcasing the genre’s signature rhythms, emotive vocals, and social commentary. The album’s centerpiece is Cliff’s anthemic title track, “The Harder They Come,” which became one of the most iconic reggae songs ever recorded.\n\nThis soundtrack holds a pivotal place in both Jimmy Cliff’s discography and the broader history of reggae. For Cliff, it marked his international breakthrough and established him as a leading voice in the genre. The album’s blend of Cliff’s original songs and key tracks from other Jamaican artists offers a comprehensive snapshot of early 1970s reggae. Upon release, the album received widespread critical acclaim for its authenticity and cultural significance, and it achieved notable commercial success, peaking at No. 140 on the US Billboard 200. Over time, it has been recognized as a foundational work in reggae and film music, celebrated for its enduring influence and historical importance.",
